# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF: an LF-only .bat breaks
# on a goto out of a block or a for loop, and does it silently.
#
# Silently is the word. cmd.exe seeks by byte offset and counts two bytes a line,
# so LF makes it resume mid-line and run the tail of a comment — `panel.bat` died
# on 'the' and 'all.bat', the ends of its own REM lines (#1225). .cmd is read by
# the same parser and needs the same thing.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
